WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.500
It's a time-honored tradition to watch horror
films in October, but spooky good times at

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.120
the movies don't have to wait until Halloween.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.430
To make sure you're keeping up with the best
new horror movies in the genre, we've got

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:16.320
a list of the best horror movies of 2018 so
far.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.060
Annihilation

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.520
Subtlety and style don't often rule the box
office, particularly when it comes to the

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:29.660
horror landscape, which is dominated by in-your-face
slashers, squeamish torture marathons, and

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.280
gritty found-footage outings.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.080
It can come as a pleasant surprise, then,
when a movie gets enough of a budget for some

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.420
striking visuals while remaining quiet enough
to leave you with lingering questions and

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.540
a genuine sense of unease.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:49.360
Alex Garland, an author and screenwriter who
made his directorial debut with the 2015 sci-fi

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.280
sleeper hit Ex Machina, returned in 2018 with
Annihilation.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:01:00.860
The movie follows a group of scientists investigating
a mysterious disaster zone filled with strange

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.440
creatures.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.160
Hailed by critics with phrases like "nightmare
fuel," Garland's sophomore effort deftly blends

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:12.460
a metaphor-laced space invasion story with
creeping dread and uncanny imagery.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.990
Though it was a financial disappointment in
theaters, word of mouth has continued to build

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.680
around Annihilation since its home release.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:24.160
Add in a cast of fan-favorite actors including
Natalie Portman, Tessa Thompson, and Oscar

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:30.380
Isaac, and Annihilation is one of the scariest
and strangest movies you'll see all year.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:36.320
"It wasn't destroying… it was changing everything.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.140
It was making something new."

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.560
Upgrade

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:46.819
In a not-too-distant future where computer-assisted
body modification is the norm, Grey, played

00:01:46.819 --> 00:01:52.110
by Logan Marshall-Green, remains staunchly
defensive of his own humanity, refusing to

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.180
become augmented.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.480
That is, until an attack leaves him wheelchair
bound and his wife dead.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.360
Enter a mysterious tech innovator who offers
to restore Grey's motor functions with his

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.620
newest AI chip.

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:09.020
As any horror aficionado could guess, this
melding of man and machine has some gruesome

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:09.520
results.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:14.860
Directed by Leigh Whannell of Saw fame and
produced by genre juggernaut Blumhouse Upgrade

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.500
blends topical concerns with an old-fashioned
sense of gritty grindhouse fun.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.100
Wildling

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:27.300
The feature debut from director Fritz Böhm,
Wildling is anchored by stunning performances

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.660
from genre favorites Brad Dourif and Liv Tyler.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.069
Bel Powley takes the lead as Anna, a teenage
girl who has grown up under the abusive thumb

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:41.320
of a father figure who claims to be protecting
her from man-eating creatures outside.

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:46.520
When she's rescued by the local sheriff, played
by Tyler, Anna begins to realize that the

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.380
stories were true… in a way.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.600
Wildling has been hailed by critics for its
powerhouse performances and striking visuals.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.700
The Hollywood Reporter listed it as one of
the ten best films debuting at South by Southwest,

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.860
and it's hard to argue with the mountain of
praise the movie has earned.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.320
"The Wildling."

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.540
"What's the wildling?"

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.620
"He eats children."

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.200
Ghost Stories

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.140
After the 1980s saw the release of the cult
favorite Creepshow, horror anthology films

00:03:18.159 --> 00:03:19.459
went mostly dormant.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:24.980
Luckily recent years have seen a revival of
the formula with Trick 'r Treat and the V/H/S

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.860
series bringing the horror anthology back
to mainstream audiences.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:35.320
In 2018, American audiences were treated to
a new British horror anthology, Ghost Stories.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.400
The project began its life as a stage play
by Andy Nyman and Jeremy Dyson, who share

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.000
writing and directing duties on the finished
film.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:49.200
The story follows a professor known for debunking
hoaxes as he investigates three cases of alleged

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.379
paranormal activity.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:56.340
The lines between reality and fiction blur
as the anthology builds to a startling surreal

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.240
climax that's absolutely jaw-dropping.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.940
A Quiet Place

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:06.150
Directed and co-written by John Krasinski,
A Quiet Place captured the attention of audiences

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:11.219
and critics when it crept into theaters in
April with a clever premise and minimalist

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:11.980
presentation.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:17.420
The film follows a family trying to survive
creatures that attack anyone who makes a sound.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.650
Krasinski anchors the film as the stoic patriarch
trying to keep his family alive in a role

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.389
about as far away from The Office's Jim Halpert
as it's possible to get.

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:32.250
The film's cast is rounded out with a stellar
performance by Emily Blunt, newcomer Noah

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.880
Jupe, and young deaf actress Millicent Simmonds,
who made sure that the film's portrayal of

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.140
a deaf child remained authentic.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.440
[Spooky music]

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.500
[Scream]

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:48.840
Cargo

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.940
With the glut of zombie fare over the past
decade, it's understandable that a drama about

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.240
the walking dead might get lost in the shuffle.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:02.020
Cargo, however, brings some fresh brains to
the sub-genre with a quiet story about one

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:05.120
family's post-outbreak life in rural Australia.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:11.720
Directed by the filmmaking team of Ben Howling
and Yolanda Ramke and anchored by an understated

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:17.380
but intense performance by Martin Freeman,
Cargo is a fitting descendent of George Romero's

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.040
original zombie films.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.420
Hereditary

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:26.919
The feature debut from writer/director Ari
Aster, Hereditary sets out to unnerve you

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:32.880
with a cornucopia of disturbing omens, bizarre
visuals, and surreal nightmare logic.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.919
Critics immediately got behind it in a big
way, heaping particular praise on the lead

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.720
performance by Toni Collette.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:45.200
She absolutely deserves the praise, giving
a performance so overcome with guilt and anger

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.080
that you're likely to be frightened even before
anything supernatural shows up.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.460
"Don't you swear at me you little s---!

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.700
Don't you ever raise your voice at me!

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.020
I am your mother!

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.760
Do you understand?"

